{"c":[{"id":"c1e11d92dfb9eca2","sum":"ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP=dead;EACCES/ESTALE stay. Claude ask; Cursor=CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT. installed_plugins.json beside cache/=cache copy not checkout; dir-mkt. --plugin-dir/synced none. orphan=version-dir+.orphaned_at. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR+CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR move plugins root.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fea602b5005e86e1","sum":"shim _alive is dead only on ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP. EACCES/ESTALE stay alive, so rectify leaves it. Path.is_file raises before 3.14 and returns False from 3.14. Claude-only fixes must not question Cursor users. sr-initialize asks only in Claude Code; Cursor uses CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261016T215531Z-cabd5aa56838fc34","text":"shim _alive: only ENOENT/ENOTDIR/ELOOP mean a baked engine is dead; other stat errors (EACCES, ESTALE) count as alive, so rectify leaves it. Do not use Path.is_file: it raises those before Python 3.14 and returns False from 3.14.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261016T222048Z-5c4cd091dd70b15f","text":"Design rule (operator, 2026-10-16): fixes for Claude Code-only problems must not add questions for Cursor users. sr-initialize asks the user only in Claude Code; Cursor keeps its own evidence (CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dc126cfe9aa69545","sum":"installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists only the cache copy, never the checkout (dir-marketplace too). --plugin-dir and synced copies: none; orphans keep version-dir plus .orphaned_at. Cursor: no record. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR move the plugins root.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261016T223043Z-086a0d75fd95fd94","text":"Claude Code proves an install by its record, not its folder: installed_plugins.json in the plugins root (beside cache/) lists each installPath; --plugin-dir (@inline) and synced copies have none; orphans keep a version-named folder plus .orphaned_at. Cursor has no such record.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T010120Z-43ea3096fec682fc","text":"Claude Code copies even directory-marketplace plugins (source ./ too) into <plugins root>/cache/<mkt>/<plugin>/<version>; installed_plugins.json there records only that copy, never the checkout. CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR both move the plugins root.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ea3fa59ce852af66","sum":"Owner outside default plugin dirs: claude if installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the exact root (before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT), else none. Local-path marketplaces load from source, not installPath. ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA}=<plugins root>/data/<id>; read paths via quoted heredoc.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0759e81a67d39207","sum":"Outside default plugin folders, claude means installed_plugins.json beside cache/ lists the exact plugin root (before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT); else no owner. A local-path marketplace caches and records a relative-path plugin, but loads it from the source folder, not installPath.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T012636Z-cb621eb5522291ae","text":"sr-initialize Step 2: an install-shaped copy outside the default plugins folders is claude when installed_plugins.json beside its cache/ holds the quoted exact plugin root (grep -qF), checked before CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT; else no owner. Supersedes the round-1 owner-rule note.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T014809Z-c4ddf9bb24e2c594","text":"Correction: relative-path plugins in a local-path Claude Code marketplace get a cache entry and an install record, but load in place from the source folder (claude plugin list --json readFromFolder). installPath is not always the folder a plugin loads from.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"477b2af74f8da1f7","sum":"CC 2.1.302 substitutes ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} in skill text: <plugins root>/data/<id>, id stockroom-inline (--plugin-dir) or stockroom-<marketplace>; 'inline' reserved. SKILL_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\" re-parses the pasted path; quoted-heredoc IFS= read -r is safe.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261017T135741Z-0a0d4ec0ff68165a","text":"Claude Code 2.1.302 substitutes ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} in plugin skill text (typed or model-invoked, prose or fence): <plugins root>/data/<id>, id stockroom-inline for --plugin-dir, stockroom-<marketplace> for installs. Marketplace name 'inline' is reserved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261017T135751Z-db7b381ea6596dc0","text":"sr-initialize Step 2: SKILL_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\" lets the shell re-parse the pasted path ($x, backtick, $(), quote pairs change it or run commands; a lone \" is a syntax error). A quoted-heredoc IFS= read -r passed all cases in dash/bash/busybox.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
